Review the uncommitted stmap38 implementation for correctness risks.

Context:
- Project policy requires numbered STMAP variants; this is stmap38.
- stmap38 adds src/base/abci/abcStmap_38.c and mapper mode 39.
- The hypothesis is to broaden first-pass SCL over-cap hotspot association beyond stmap37's root/immediate-fanin set by adding nearby fanins, downstream fanout users, and candidate cut-leaf hotspot checks before applying local SCL feedback.
- Existing map and stmap0 through stmap37 behavior should remain buildable and comparable.

Focus:
- command registration and build integration
- fSkipFanout mode-range plumbing
- mapper counter isolation for mode 39
- lifetime and reset of Map_Stmap38SetSclLoadFeedback pointers
- whether mode 39 can affect non-stmap38 commands
- diagnostic accuracy and any memory/lifetime hazards
- any missed correctness or reproducibility issue in the runtime artifacts

