## version37 / stmap37

- hypothesis: First-pass direct SCL over-cap hotspots can be mapped back to original AIG IDs and used as a local feedback set, so the final mapper penalizes only high-reference strong seeds that are spatially near measured downstream load offenders.
- motivation: `stmap36` proved that direct SCL load feedback can alter mapper decisions, but its aggregate scalar blocked the known `syn2` strong seed globally without improving final downstream `stime`. `stmap37` tests whether localizing that feedback to first-pass over-cap roots and their immediate mapped fanin cone is a safer discriminator.
- command name: `stmap37`
- files changed:
  - `src/base/abci/abc.c`
  - `src/base/abci/abcStmap_37.c`
  - `src/base/abci/module.make`
  - `abclib.dsp`
  - `src/map/mapper/mapperInt.h`
  - `src/map/mapper/mapperCore.c`
  - `src/map/mapper/mapperMatch.c`
  - `.autoeda/runtime/results/stmap37/*`
  - `.autoeda/runtime/versions.md`
  - `.autoeda/runtime/campaign_state.json`
  - `.autoeda/runtime/last_prompt.txt`
- algorithm summary: `stmap37` keeps the classic SCL-genlib gain default of `250`. The command first maps with mapper mode `36`, preserving the observational direct SCL load surface from `stmap35`, then measures each mapped node's SCL fanout input-pin load divided by its Liberty `max_out_cap`. Over-cap mapped roots and their immediate mapped fanin cone are translated through `vOrigNodeIds` into original AIG IDs, sorted by local load ratio, and capped at `64` hotspots. The command then remaps with mapper mode `38`. Mode 38 keeps the continuous moderate-seed penalty and the bounded drive-normalized strong-seed penalty, but adds an extra SCL term only when the current mapper node's AIG ID appears in the first-pass hotspot set with ratio greater than `1.0`. The feedback globals are reset after the final map. Existing `map` and `stmap0` through `stmap36` remain on their prior command paths and mode numbers.
- validation run:
  - build: `make ABC_USE_NO_READLINE=1` passed and produced `./abc`. Log: `.autoeda/runtime/results/stmap37/build.log`.
  - help: `./abc -c "stmap37 -h"` printed usage text with default `-G 250.00` and local SCL hotspot feedback enabled. Log: `.autoeda/runtime/results/stmap37/help.log`.
  - smoke: `read_lib 7nm_lvt_ff.lib; read benchmarks/i10.aig; resyn; resyn2; dch -v; stmap37; topo; buffer; upsize -v; dnsize -v; stime` passed with final delay `198.64 ps`, area `1303.10`, inactive feedback severity `0.000`, and six selected local hotspots. Log: `.autoeda/runtime/results/stmap37/smoke_i10.log`.
  - full evaluation artifacts: `.autoeda/runtime/results/stmap37/summary.json`, `metrics.csv`, `comparison.csv`, `guard_stats.csv`, `early_seed_stats.csv`, `near_miss_stats.csv`, `penalty_stats.csv`, `scl_load_stats.csv`, `feedback_load_stats.csv`, `feedback_stats.csv`, `hotspot_stats.csv`, `feedback_load_top.csv`, `hotspot_top.csv`, penalty diagnostic CSVs, raw baseline/candidate logs, CEC temporaries, CEC logs, CEC summary, review logs, review summary, artifact check, and version-log check.
