The source-level stmap38 plumbing appears isolated, but the tracked campaign state is left in a transient running state that can break reproducible resume/automation behavior. This should be corrected before the patch is considered ready.

Review comment:

- [P2] Reset live campaign status before committing — /Users/cunxiy/Documents/research/autoresearch-eda/abc-harness/.autoeda/runtime/campaign_state.json:9-9
  If these runtime artifacts are committed or used to resume the campaign, `status: "agent-running"` points at a stale launcher/PID while `last_completed_version` still says `stmap37` even though the patch adds `stmap38` results. That can make the harness think an agent is already active or resume from the wrong iteration; finalize the state for the completed stmap38 run or keep this transient launch state out of the patch.
